# Pairs with EventualConvergence. A drained entry leaves the buffer without
# being merged - a drained apply that fails and is neither retried nor
# dead-lettered (DrainBufferAsync dead-letters it). The entry was acknowledged
# when it was parked, so nothing re-sends it.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceDrainDropsReleasedEntry
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a drained entry is removed from the buffer without being applied
PERTURBS: Drain

--- FIND
               /\ val' = Merged(x, r)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the released entry is not merged.
               /\ val' = val
--- END
